{"w":2400,"h":3209,"lines":[{"x":0.097087377716845488,"c":1,"t":"Sample Writing answers","y":0.042056074712006231,"w":0.23106796264648438,"h":0.016199376947040434},{"y":0.08990117643379314,"c":1,"w":0.36334960937500005,"h":0.023973007439824334,"x":0.09892089104919681,"t":"TEST 4, WRITING TASK 2"},{"h":0.017518836761189482,"y":0.12928348892549923,"w":0.80582524617513029,"c":1,"t":"This model has been prepared by an examiner as an example of a very good answer.","x":0.097087376911850071},{"w":0.80582524617513018,"c":1,"h":0.020385966791170884,"x":0.097087376856903801,"y":0.15843023202918771,"t":"The population in most parts of the world is ageing; people are living longer and there are tewer"},{"c":1,"x":0.096974936289617994,"t":"younger people in many places as birth rates fall. This phenomenon has pros and cons, but this","y":0.17844483415453027,"w":0.79631632486979165,"h":0.022832549621011666},{"x":0.097087383747951894,"w":0.78252426147460941,"c":1,"t":"essay will contend that, on balance, the advantages of having an older population outweigh the","h":0.020395023429133796,"y":0.20203488319268248},{"x":0.096785807359972678,"y":0.22505126775529694,"h":0.018640525318751822,"c":1,"w":0.085679766337076815,"t":"negatives."},{"c":1,"y":0.25290697621392355,"h":0.020348838259497848,"t":"The first issue that occurs to many people when considering the ageing population is the expense. If","x":0.097087377915829234,"w":0.83106796264648441},{"t":"people live longer, they may have more than 30 years of retirement and may need to be supported","y":0.27373173696116637,"h":0.021947046678014281,"c":1,"x":0.097016897549364392,"w":0.82538884480794283},{"c":1,"y":0.29422909714025702,"t":"tinancially by the government or their families. If they experience age-related illness, this impacts","x":0.096979848590375187,"w":0.81575169881184884,"h":0.023781413378373806},{"h":0.020386873524508409,"t":"the health system and takes up resources needed by other people in society. What's more, when","x":0.09708738035860591,"y":0.31682242931969029,"w":0.79417475382486979,"c":1},{"y":0.33862928381648016,"h":0.020382344611337366,"c":1,"x":0.097087371424038532,"w":0.76699030558268222,"t":"older people are financially independent, it might be hard for younger people if they have to"},{"t":"compete to get a foot in the door of the housing market or gain employment.","c":1,"w":0.64854370117187499,"x":0.097087372569402253,"y":0.36043613710875588,"h":0.020377816886545386},{"h":0.020560747663551315,"w":0.80388351440429684,"t":"That being said, older people have a lot to contribute in terms of wisdom, experience and skills.","c":1,"y":0.38940809976187485,"x":0.097087369136659357},{"w":0.80582524617513029,"h":0.020560747663551315,"c":1,"y":0.41121495307419087,"x":0.099029124424288573,"t":"Many people are active and productive for longer than their counterparts were 50 years ago and"},{"x":0.09708737685798989,"w":0.80582524617513029,"c":1,"y":0.43302180637976828,"t":"are an asset to the economy and society well into their old age. They are able to work for longer","h":0.020560747663551315},{"w":0.81758341471354157,"c":1,"t":"and after retirement they contribute in many ways too, such as by doing charitable work, spending","h":0.023014726965598253,"x":0.098974623147744009,"y":0.45342166853573407},{"y":0.4748938716112352,"w":0.76909245808919269,"h":0.023157871995016732,"c":1,"t":"money as consumers and supporting their families. Grandparents often care for their young","x":0.098942354508445574},{"t":"grandchildren, making it easier for both parents to work.","h":0.020560747663551426,"c":1,"w":0.4757281494140625,"x":0.099029129053787551,"y":0.49844236748281201},{"w":0.80404210408528642,"t":"While it is true that an ageing population poses challenges for governments, it is clear that these","h":0.022089256452994199,"y":0.52664137053695592,"c":1,"x":0.098957217880017087},{"h":0.022342068681093008,"c":1,"w":0.6448151652018228,"x":0.09893663919180147,"t":"are outweighed by the significant benefits that elderly people bring to society.","y":0.5481586786676117},{"x":0.10097087022353482,"y":0.58866279040370373,"c":1,"t":"Here are comments from another examiner:","w":0.41165049235026041,"h":0.014534884301301454},{"t":"This is a good response to the task. Both sides of the argument are presented,","c":1,"x":0.1456310597154038,"w":0.7417475891113281,"h":0.017519742306147723,"y":0.6249221182671898},{"y":0.64236760150079819,"c":1,"w":0.77864079793294261,"x":0.14563105748852734,"h":0.017516119532124619,"t":"with the ideas extended for both. The candidate makes their position clear from the"},{"t":"beginning, that there are more advantages than disadvantages.","h":0.017583134018372082,"c":1,"y":0.6627906975605683,"w":0.59999999999999998,"x":0.14563106786076788},{"h":0.017504346853476016,"t":"The second paragraph addresses the expense of looking after the elderly, the","c":1,"x":0.14563106317154145,"y":0.69906542069655508,"w":0.73009709676106782},{"c":1,"t":"health system and the cost for governments. It also captures the challenge that","w":0.74580464680989567,"x":0.14556919388669495,"y":0.71653135619442088,"h":0.020202440636180263},{"c":1,"x":0.14757281147243731,"t":"older people take up houses and jobs so younger people cannot progress.","h":0.017441860686210009,"y":0.73691860453776592,"w":0.69902913411458334},{"w":0.78446604410807286,"h":0.017488951994994006,"t":"The third paragraph presents the advantages of the [wisdom, experience and skills]","x":0.14757280321626362,"y":0.77320872252920259,"c":1},{"w":0.77292292277018226,"h":0.020009042615088291,"t":"older people can bring: that they are more active and remain productive for longer,","c":1,"x":0.14751232695604907,"y":0.79011836761115561},{"w":0.76699030558268222,"c":1,"t":"not only working, but also [doing charitable work, spending money as consumers,","y":0.81090342649751757,"x":0.1456310606675956,"h":0.017584945702478483},{"w":0.68737864176432295,"t":"supporting their families and even grandchildren for the working parents].","x":0.14757281495075802,"y":0.82834890973617492,"h":0.017581322928455378,"c":1},{"w":0.52621358235677085,"h":0.015988371899566256,"c":1,"x":0.14563107326821656,"t":"This means that the conclusion is relevant and justified.","y":0.86627906984640557},{"c":1,"w":0.036893202463785801,"y":0.95784883706693136,"x":0.10097087445213182,"h":0.01308139551465759,"t":"136"}]}